---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import MotionFilm from "../components/MotionFilm.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About | Oliver Hitchings"
  description="About Oliver Hitchings and the practical engineering approach behind inspectable automation systems."
>
  <main class="subpage about-page">
    <section class="about-hero" data-about-hero>
      <div class="container about-hero__grid">
        <div class="about-hero__copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">About Oliver Hitchings</p>
          <h1>I design small automation systems around the work people already do.</h1>
          <p class="about-hero__intro">
            My approach starts with the task: what triggers it, which evidence it uses, where
            judgement is needed and who owns the result.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="about-hero__visual">
          <MotionFilm film="feature-card" class="about-hero__film">
            <Fragment slot="caption">
              <aside
                class="about-identity"
                aria-label="Oliver Hitchings working focus"
                data-about-identity
              >
                <p data-field="Name">Oliver Hitchings</p>
                <p data-field="Focus">Automation systems</p>
                <p data-field="Sequence">Map → Build → Hand over</p>
              </aside>
            </Fragment>
          </MotionFilm>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section
      class="container editorial-section about-stance"
      data-operating-stance
      data-reveal
    >
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Operating stance</p>
        <h2>The model call is only one step.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="about-stance__copy">
        The operational questions come first: which source of truth wins, when the system should
        stop, what gets logged and what a person should do when confidence is low. Once those
        boundaries are clear, the build can stay narrow, observable and easier to hand over.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section
      class="container editorial-section about-principles"
      data-about-principles
      data-reveal
    >
      <div class="editorial-heading compact-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Operating principles</p>
          <h2>Four rules for an operable system.</h2>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="about-principle-rows">
        <article>
          <span aria-hidden="true">01</span>
          <h3>Show the work</h3>
          <p>Prompts, rules, assumptions and logs visible enough to review a bad run.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span aria-hidden="true">02</span>
          <h3>Keep a person responsible</h3>
          <p>Stop for review when a step is uncertain or consequential.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span aria-hidden="true">03</span>
          <h3>Design the failure path</h3>
          <p>Make retries, stop conditions and escalation explicit.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span aria-hidden="true">04</span>
          <h3>Hand over ownership</h3>
          <p>Leave run instructions, logs and change notes with the owner.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about-final-cta" data-about-cta>
      <div class="container about-final-cta__grid">
        <p class="eyebrow">A useful starting point</p>
        <div>
          <h2>Bring one task that already repeats.</h2>
          <p class="about-cta__copy">
            Describe the trigger, inputs, output, tools and reviewer. That is enough to decide
            whether a Task Map, First Build or Operator System is the sensible starting point.
          </p>
          <div class="cta-row left">
            <a class="button ghost" href="/services#packages">View packages</a>
            <a class="button" href="/services#contact">Start an enquiry</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
